# .packagingignore — paths that must NEVER be copied into a packaged build.
#
# Why this file exists: .gitignore protects COMMITS, not a packager that copies
# the working tree. This is the authoritative exclusion list for L3 packaging and
# later installer work, committed so the packager inherits it.
#
# Rules are repo-root-relative globs, one per line — plain exclusions only.
# There are deliberately NO `!` re-include rules: negation semantics differ
# between packing tools, so section 4 states what must be kept in prose instead.
# A packager MUST apply these exclusions BEFORE copying anything.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. SECRETS — never ship.
#    These carry live credentials: the Postgres password, the SUPER_ADMIN
#    unlock secret, the OTP pepper, and per-machine local config. The packaged
#    application generates its own secrets at first run.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.freebuff/super-admin-credentials.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. LIVE DATA + UNSANITIZED BACKUPS — never ship.
#    CRITICAL: .pg/backups holds pre-reset copies containing REAL Argon2id
#    password hashes (users.json), session token hashes, and reset code/ticket
#    hashes, plus a 66 MB physical cluster copy of the pre-reset dataset.
#    pnk-dev / pnk-test are live development and test data directories.
#    A fresh install must initdb an EMPTY cluster and apply migrations.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pg/backups/**
.pg/pnk-dev/**
.pg/pnk-test/**
.pg/*.log
.pg/*.err

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. DEVELOPMENT / TOOLING ARTIFACTS — never ship.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.freebuff/**
# a previously packaged build must never nest inside a new one
dist/**
.next/cache/**
.next/dev/**
.next/trace
.next-dev.log
.pg/l2-probe.mjs
.pg/l2-probe-seed.mjs
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
node_modules/.cache/**
**/.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. DO NOT OVER-EXCLUDE — these ARE part of the package.
#
#    The exclusions in sections 1-3 are deliberately narrow. Do NOT widen them
#    into blanket rules such as `.pg/**` or `.tools/**` (or `node_modules/**`,
#    `.next/**` blanket-wide): the runtime needs parts of all of those trees.
#
#    REQUIRED — must be present in the packaged build:
#      .tools/node/**        bundled portable Node 22 runtime
#      .pg/pgsql/**          bundled portable PostgreSQL 16 binaries
#                            (exclude only its data dirs and backups, above)
#      package.json, package-lock.json, next.config.ts, tsconfig.json
#      public/**             static assets
#      src/app/fonts/**      vendored fonts (no network fetch at runtime)
#      drizzle/**            migrations + drizzle.config.ts, applied at first run
#      the Next.js production build output
#
#    node_modules: install/refresh it with the lockfile at package time rather
#    than copying it blindly — only the traced production dependency set belongs
#    in the package (e.g. an `output: "standalone"` build).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
